{"p4": {"friction": "depends-on with the head's own conclusion as the tail (c18, Remark 2.23: \"It is a consequence of the classification of Dirac operators ... that color is unbroken\") fits neither wrong-direction nor wrong-relation cleanly.", "doubt": "c13 hinges on how to read 'otherwise'; c15's coefficient grouping is loose against (3.41), which is truncated in the input; c18 is the wrong-direction vs wrong-relation choice.", "missing_context": "Theorem 3.13's eq. (3.41) is cut off mid-formula, and the earlier introduction of C_3 (before Prop. 2.24) is not in the input.", "proposed_change": "Add to depends-on: 'If the tail is the head's own conclusion and reversing does not give a valid edge, grade wrong-relation.'", "process_observation": "This paper's own claims c12 and c19 appear as rubric examples and near-misses, so grading them partly echoes the rubric rather than testing it independently."}}
